CompareBaseline|Baseline A|The reference snapshot used to describe additions, removals and changes in the candidate. A baseline is not automatically trusted or safe.|Choose the earlier or known reference build here. When comparison opens from a loaded editor document, A includes that document's current in-memory bytes, including unsaved edits.|Comparison does not overwrite the baseline. Choosing a different reference reverses the meaning of added and removed; use a trustworthy source when investigating an unexpected change.
CompareCandidate|Candidate B|The second file, whose structure and bytes are compared against baseline A. Candidate means the file being examined, not a verdict about its safety.|Choose the later build or altered copy. Read the path labels before comparing, then inspect differences and their reasons in the findings table.|The file is read as data and never executed by comparison. A different file hash proves different bytes, but does not identify why they differ or whether the change is harmful.
