Field|Field|A named numeric member of a PE structure, with a specific byte location and fixed storage width.|Use the field name, group and contextual help together; the same name can mean different things in COFF, section and directory records.|Editing changes exactly those bytes. A field's valid range depends on its width and on the surrounding structure, not only its numeric type.
Value|Value|The numeric interpretation of a field's bytes, displayed in a form suitable for comparison and editing.|Use hexadecimal to compare masks and addresses with specifications, or decimal when working with counts and sizes.|PE numeric fields use little-endian storage, so displayed hex digits need not appear in the same left-to-right order in the file's hex view.
Offset|File offset|A zero-based byte position measured from the beginning of the file on disk.|Use a field's offset to locate its storage in Hex or compare a change with an external format description.|It is not automatically a loaded memory address or RVA. Replacing bytes at an offset affects that disk position without moving the surrounding contents.
