Group|Group|Identifies a field's owning structure. DOS means legacy Disk Operating System; COFF means Common Object File Format. The optional header is historically named and required for PE images.|Use groups to disambiguate names: COFF Characteristics describes the image; section Characteristics describes a section's attributes.|The group is a display label. Editing a value does not rename or move its containing structure.
SectionName|Section name|An eight-byte ASCII label in a section header, often .text or .data.|Use conventional names as clues, then verify with permissions, ranges and directory mappings. A producer can choose different names or combine contents.|Renaming changes only the label. It does not convert data to code, update references or guarantee that all tools treat the renamed section identically.
